SK 409 REFP loaders, Init with Guards, C1 Extract, D2 Build, D2 Extract and others) and the child's Library Check (ASK 422a). Engine Code text 3,577,507 to 3,432,407 characters; child 1,134,191 to 1,119,909.\n    - Not changed: the Shared Library in both workflows (lib_sha c91b9f1489e9c132, map_sha 99d7d2c673d59735), Alternate Build and Early Alternate Build (byte-equal; they keep their comments), every other node type, every connection, prompt and model setting. gate/pack.cjs and STUBV are unchanged: the stubs were edited as text.\n    - Shown offline: in every changed node the token stream and syntax tree are equal, the code compiles in an async wrapper, no comment is left, and the set of literal $() names is equal; every edited stub rebuilds (unpack.cjs rebuild) to a byte-equal source, 44 of 44; ASK 385 check PASS. The reasoning guard flagged one node, Alternate Merge (the word \"reasoning\" in a removed ASK 297 comment); the operator's card press allowed it. Not run: the replay gate, because no saved run inputs exist; it would run the same tokens on both sides.\n    - Live: engine 06967796 (from b780b2ae), saved 03:14:41Z on 11-19; child e1f2b1c4 (from 7b043bab), saved 03:14:45Z on 11-19; lib_sha c91b9f1489e9c132 on both.\n    - Limits: not shown by a run; its mark is no \"pkgLIB:\" or \"pkgLIB1\" stop and lib422 naming c91b9f1489e9c132. A full repack by gate/pack.cjs at STUBV 3 writes the stub header comments back. Old package scripts that find stubs by the \"// pkgLIB stub\" header find none; a stub is found by its run line. Every later build anchors on the comment-free text.\n  - THE OPENING VERDICT WORD OF A RECOMPUTED JUDGMENT IS REPLACED (pkgRHD, ASK 297; Alternate Merge):"}]$p$::jsonb,'93ef564e8accad8e0096a81697c7fa61',585725,$q$Engine manual v197: ASK 428 code comments removed$q$,$q$Adds the ASK 428 entry (code comments removed from engine and child Code nodes, carrying ASK 422(b)); section 15 Comments bullet and the REFP loader line updated.$q$,$q$v197 